# Response headers for hosts that read this file (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages).
# GitHub Pages serves no custom headers and will simply ignore it; the page's
# own <meta> Content-Security-Policy still applies everywhere, so nothing here
# is load-bearing for the privacy guarantee. These are the two protections a
# meta tag cannot express.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
